Platformer Project - Calvin Richards, Keyan Premji

LAYERS: 
    ground, background, decoration, hazard, object
    Tile size of 32px

Every tile can have its own properties, for instance in Tiled you can select some spikes and give them
the special property "damage" which you can then read in phaser. Objects have their own special values.

SCENES:
    Start, Playing, End 

PLAYER MOVEMENT:
    Acceleration for holding direction, eventual max speed
    press space to jump, that needs acceleration too
    press s to switch gravity

SPECIAL GAME MECHANICS: gravity switching and moving platforms! Will there be enemies? If so then there should be 
attacking mechanics, jumping on their heads? powerups like fire flower in mario?

item pickups: coins (increase score by +1) and diamonds (increase player speed allowing for parkour skips)

Should use animations, will figure out more after the "juice" lecture. 
Added particle animations for constant player movement AND explosive particle animation for switching gravity

Moving platforms add some difficulty because the player does not automatically stick to them, requiring extra 
precise input from the player.
The dangerous spikes make level traversal significantly more difficult and encourage use of the gravity switching mechanic.

OPTIONAL ELEMENTS:
Complex Camera
Not necessarily double jumping but gravity switch :)
Ways for player to die 
Power-Up



FILE LAYOUT:
    player.js handles all player functions, that means it will receive flags
    movement, health management, etc...

REPOSITORY:
Below is the shared repository where you can view changes, commit history, etc...
https://github.com/CalviRichi/Phaser-Platformer 
    
